# 7. Example of the improved customer experience

### Before

A customer notices that an order has not arrived, checks the app, contacts chat, repeats the order number, receives a generic apology, and is told to wait. After contacting support again, the customer receives a different delivery estimate and still has no clear owner.

### After

The system identifies that the order is at risk and sends a local-language message before the promised delivery time has passed. The customer selects a revised delivery date or refund through a simple link. If the issue remains unresolved, the case is assigned to a named service owner. The agent sees the order history, communicates a realistic deadline, and can approve an appropriate remedy without seeking several internal approvals. A follow-up message confirms the outcome.

The difference is not merely faster response. It is reduced effort, clearer accountability, and a stronger perception that the company is taking responsibility.

